 "note": "Read by eye from every film frame (frame pixels). head and waist: per frame, the head centre and the waist (top of the white wrap, centre); frames 2-5 were evened out so the walk to the ladder goes the same distance each frame, and frames 28-37 are set so the waist keeps rising along the drawn ladder at a slowing rate (about 6 px a frame down to 2) and ends just below the rail tops, since the drawn ladder is shorter than the film's. make_scene.py keeps the torso one fixed length (shrinking up to 7 % from frame 24 as the man recedes) and moves the waist onto the middle of the drawn ladder. start and moves: each hand and foot is held where it was put until it moves; a move is [frame lifted, frame put down, target], at least 3 frames on the ladder, the top foot steps 5-6 frames. On the ground a target is a frame point; on the ladder ['rung', i, u] (rung i of the drawn ladder from the bottom, u along it from the left rail), ['rail', r, u], or ['at', r, a] (rail r at height a up the ladder, a hand gripping the rail). Hands go up the rails alternately, each grip about 30-50 px above the shoulder when it is taken; they end on the tops of the two rails. Feet go up the rungs one at a time. make_scene.py rejects any frame where limbs cross each other or the rails, an arm or leg folds, a joint moves more than 9 px from the last frame (other than the stepping hand or foot), or a bone changes length by more than a few % beyond what its foreshortening allows.",
